10	 * signatures, so it is loaded by RECIPIENTS in external inboxes (Gmail image
11	 * proxy, Outlook, Apple Mail) that have no Nxeon session. There is therefore no
12	 * auth here. The exposure is limited: `id` is an unguessable cuid (never a
13	 * filename, so no path traversal), and the response only ever returns stored
14	 * image bytes with an allow-listed image Content-Type — never HTML/JS, and a
15	 * `default-src 'none'; sandbox` CSP + nosniff prevent it executing as a document.
